! fcc aluminium with its cell doubled along `a3`, so that two atoms sit in it
! and the `Gamma`-point dynamical matrix has something in it: the modes of this
! cell at `Gamma` are the primitive cell's at `Gamma` **and** at the zone-boundary
! point the doubling folds in, so three of the six frequencies are acoustic and
! three are not.
!
! Same pseudopotential, cutoff and smearing as `al-metal.in`, which is QE's own
! `pw_metal/metal.in` -- only the cell and the k-grid differ, so what this adds
! over that file is the *second atom* and nothing else.
!
! `nosym` on an **unshifted** grid, which is the combination a response can be
! computed on without symmetrising it (`si-epsilon-unshifted-nosym.in` records
! the same choice for silicon). It is also what `ph.x` needs here: with the
! symmetry on it refuses the cell outright -- "FFT grid incompatible with
! symmetry" out of `phq_setup` -- so the reference in
! `reference.out.ph-al2-metal` is a `nosym` run and this input is the one that
! generated it.
!
! `ph.x` gives 1.1, 1.8, 1.9, 146.7, 146.7 and 311.0 cm^-1: three acoustic modes
! at the sum rule's own residue and three the doubling folds in from the zone
! boundary.
!
! This file was committed for a phase that had not happened yet: P24c put the
! metallic *response* in and left the second derivative refused, and 1.9 against
! the 155.7 the unguarded assembly returned was the measurement behind that
! refusal. P28 lifted it -- the electronic half of the `jvp` takes `wk` where
! the frozen Hessian keeps `wg`, because a metal's `dpsi` already carries its
! occupation -- and the same six modes now come out at 0.700, 1.607, 1.725,
! 146.7093, 146.7132 and 311.0335, which is 0.0019 cm^-1 on the three real ones.
! So this is the phase's *check met* rather than its target
! (`tests/regression/test_phonons.py`).
!
! The folded pair splits by 0.0039 here and by 0.0039 in `ph.x`, and that
! near-degeneracy is the sharp part: this input is `nosym`, so nothing
! symmetrises the assembled matrix and the splitting has to come out of the
! calculation. It read as an *exact* degeneracy (146.711240 twice) until P28a
! found that `symdynph_gq` was being applied to a `nosym` run after all, and a
! group average flattens precisely this.
 &control
    calculation='scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav=0, celldm(1)=7.50,
    nat=2, ntyp=1,
    ecutwfc=15.0, nosym=.true., noinv=.true.,
    occupations='smearing', smearing='marzari-vanderbilt', degauss=0.05
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-12
 /
CELL_PARAMETERS alat
  -0.50  0.00  0.50
   0.00  0.50  0.50
  -1.00  1.00  0.00
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Al  26.98 Al.pz-vbc.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (alat)
 Al  0.00  0.00  0.00
 Al -0.50  0.50  0.00
K_POINTS automatic
 4 4 2 0 0 0
